# Invention No. 5 in E-flat major, BWV 776 (J. S. Bach)
#
# Character: stately and ornate. The subject is a slow line in eighths
# and quarters, each note dressed with a mordent, rising by step over
# two bars; against it the other hand runs a busy sixteenth-note
# countersubject. The two trade places throughout. It wants a broad,
# unhurried pulse in four, the subject singing over the running notes.
#
# Time signature: 4/4, 32 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI;
# the first note (the bass E-flat) is on the downbeat of bar 1.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 88, 128 quarters, about 1:30.
# Track times: Glenn Gould (Sony, 1964) 1:21, about 95; Angela Hewitt
# (Hyperion) 1:21, about 95; Andras Schiff (ECM, clavichord) 1:25,
# about 90; Gustav Leonhardt (harpsichord, Apple Music reissue) 2:01,
# about 63, a slow outlier. 88 sits just under the three pianists who
# agree, so the mordents and sixteenths stay clear on the chip.
#
# Structure (read from the Mutopia score and checked against the MIDI;
# the key plan is my own reading, no published bar-by-bar analysis was
# used):
#   1-2    Subject, top, E-flat, over the bass's running countersubject.
#   3-4    Continuation, top; the hands exchange the running figure.
#   5-6    Subject, bottom, on B-flat; the top has the countersubject.
#   7-8    Continuation, on B-flat 7.
#   9-11   Subject, top, as a rising sequence (on E-flat, C, D), heading
#          for C minor.
#   12-13  Subject, bottom, C minor.
#   14-15  Continuation, to C7 (15): the dominant of F minor.
#   16-17  Subject, top, F minor.
#   18-19  Continuation, to F7.
#   20-22  Subject, bottom, as a falling sequence (B-flat minor, A-flat,
#          G).
#   23-24  Subject, top, on A-flat and B-flat.
#   25-26  Subject, bottom, E-flat.
#   27-28  Subject, top, E-flat: the opening returns.
#   29-32  Continuation as in 3-4, extended; final cadence in E-flat
#          with a turn and a fermata.

tempo 88

voice mid 0          # two voices only: there is no middle voice to set back

dyn 1 mf             # bars 1-8: the exposition in E-flat and B-flat
lead 1-2 top         # subject, top, over the running bass
lead 5-6 bottom      # subject, bass, on B-flat

dyn 9 mp             # bars 9-15: the rising sequence toward C minor,
                     # a softer manual
lead 9-11 top        # the subject's rising sequence, top
lead 12-13 bottom    # subject, bass, C minor
broaden 15 0.95      # bar 15: a breath on C7 before F minor

dyn 16 mf            # bars 16-26: F minor and the way home
lead 16-17 top       # subject, top, F minor
lead 20-22 bottom    # the bass's falling sequence of subject entries
lead 23-24 top       # subject, top, on A-flat and B-flat
lead 25-26 bottom    # subject, bass, E-flat

dyn 27 f             # bars 27-32: the opening returns, full
lead 27-28 top       # subject, top, E-flat

rit 2 0.7            # bars 31-32 into the final E-flat
